# The realtime image builds with the REPO ROOT as context (it needs shared/),
# so this file guards what gets shipped to the Docker daemon from the root.
#
# .env is the important line: secrets must never enter a build context —
# anything in the context can end up in an image layer, and image layers
# leak (registries, cache exports, `docker history`).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
dist
coverage
.git
.github
*.md
